===============================================================================
RETEST: Scenario 02 - PgBouncer Connection Pool Exhaustion
Date: 2026-06-20
===============================================================================

BUG FOUND AND FIXED:
  validate.sh line 69 - awk '{print $4}' assumed space-delimited output,
  but PgBouncer SHOW POOLS uses pipe-delimited format. Fixed to:
    awk -F'|' '{gsub(/[ \t]/,"",$3); print $3}'
  This was causing baseline to FAIL with "syntax error: operand expected"

STEP 1: Baseline Validate (expect PASS)
-----------------------------------------
Result (before fix): FAIL - Check 3 parse error (bug)
Result (after fix): PASS (4/4)
  Check 1: PgBouncer port 6432 open on 100.26.54.122 - PASS
  Check 2: Query through PgBouncer in 0s - PASS
  Check 3: cl_active = 0 (not saturated) - PASS
  Check 4: PostgreSQL on primary healthy - PASS

STEP 2: Inject Chaos
---------------------
Action: Flooded PgBouncer with 200 connections holding advisory locks
Result: Pool exhausted (inject script's test connection timed out - exit 124)
Note: inject.sh timed out at the saturation-check step because the fresh
      connection queued forever. This confirms injection worked.

STEP 3: Validate After Inject (expect FAIL)
---------------------------------------------
Result: FAIL (3 PASS, 1 FAIL) - detection works correctly
  Check 1: PgBouncer port 6432 open - PASS
  Check 2: Query through PgBouncer in 0s - PASS (transaction pooling lets some through)
  Check 3: cl_active = 50 (saturated, threshold is 50) - FAIL (correct)
  Check 4: PostgreSQL primary healthy - PASS

Note: In transaction pooling mode, short queries can still execute between
      transactions even while pool is flooded. Check 3 (cl_active count)
      is the reliable detection mechanism.

STEP 4: Restore
-----------------
Action: pkill -f 'pg_advisory_lock' + systemctl restart pgbouncer on primary
Wait: 5 seconds after restart

STEP 5: Final Validate (expect PASS)
--------------------------------------
Result: PASS (4/4)
  Check 1: PgBouncer port 6432 open - PASS
  Check 2: Query through PgBouncer in 1s - PASS
  Check 3: cl_active = 0 (not saturated) - PASS
  Check 4: PostgreSQL primary healthy - PASS

===============================================================================
VERDICT: Scenario 02 inject/validate cycle - ALL STEPS PASSED (after bug fix)
  - Baseline: PASS (after fixing awk parsing bug)
  - Detection after inject: correctly detected saturation (1 FAIL)
  - Restore: successful
